The problem was that serial.block() is called before serial.open() in hydro branch kobuki_driver/kobuki.cpp line 93

```
  serial.block(4000); // blocks by default, but just to be clear!
  try {
    serial.open(parameters.device_port, ecl::BaudRate_115200, ecl::DataBits_8, ecl::StopBits_1, ecl::NoParity);  // this will throw exceptions - NotFoundError, OpenError
    is_connected = true;
  }
```

In the version 0.3.9, which I confirmed that working fine,  the block() was called after open().
